# A green full verification over HEAD empties the derived debt.
#
# The fixture builds a throwaway Ze checkout with a bare upstream, commits one
# change, and asserts the REAL `le commit debt-status` exits 1 (owed). It then
# runs verify.Run, the lifecycle `le verify worktree` answers through, with a
# fixture action runner that answers every stage green: a native run over the
# real population takes this machine's job slots for most of an hour. It
# asserts the green record sits at the asking root naming HEAD, uncut, and that
# `le commit debt-status` then exits 0.
#
# Spec: plan/post-release/engineering/spec-verification-debt-derived.md (AC-8, AC-25).
# Delete the green-record write from the lifecycle (internal/le/verify/lifecycle.go)
# and seq=1 fails at green-record-at-asking-root.

option=timeout:value=120s

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=le test fixture runner/verify-green-record-clears-derived-debt
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:contains=debt-owed-before-verify
expect=stdout:contains=green-record-at-asking-root
expect=stdout:contains=derived-debt-cleared
